---
export const title = 'Keyboard and accessibility';
export const order = 500;
---

<p>
  Menus follow the disclosure navigation pattern, not the ARIA menu pattern. The links are ordinary
  links and stay in the Tab order, so the header reads and behaves like the navigation of any
  website.
</p>

<table class='docs-table'>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Key</th><th>Where</th><th>Does</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Anywhere</td><td>Moves through the skip link, the brand, the links and menu buttons, an open panel's links, then the actions. Leaving an open panel closes it.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd> / <kbd>Space</kbd></td><td>Menu button</td><td>Opens or closes the panel.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Arrow Down</kbd></td><td>Menu button</td><td>Opens the panel and moves to its first link.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Arrow Down</kbd> / <kbd>Arrow Up</kbd></td><td>Panel</td><td>Moves to the next or previous link, wrapping around.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Home</kbd> / <kbd>End</kbd></td><td>Panel</td><td>Moves to the first or last link.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Escape</kbd></td><td>Panel</td><td>Closes it and returns focus to the menu button.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Escape</kbd></td><td>Drawer</td><td>Closes the drawer and returns focus to the menu button.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<ul>
  <li>The bar is the page's banner landmark and the links are in a named navigation landmark.</li>
  <li>A menu button has <code>aria-expanded</code> and <code>aria-controls</code>; the current link has <code>aria-current="page"</code>.</li>
  <li>The drawer is a modal dialog: the page behind it is inert and focus stays inside until it closes.</li>
  <li>The skip link, the menu button's and close button's names and the landmark's name are Peacock strings, translated with <code>setPeacockStrings()</code>.</li>
</ul>
